# {{ .prefix }}-reviewing-impl

This skill owns independent assurance only, never effort creation, checkpoints, integration, pending artifact transitions, topology removal, retrospective, or finish.

<!-- awf:include implementation-autonomy -->

<!-- awf:section when-fires -->
## When this skill fires

Skip review only for a locally obvious, low-risk, directly verified change where an independent reviewer is unlikely to uncover meaningful hidden consequences. Review is required for meaningful breadth, non-obvious logic, contract or compatibility effects, migrations, security, concurrency, data-loss risk, or verification requiring substantive judgment. Uncertainty resolves toward review. Artifact-only changes use the same risk judgment.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section sha-range-detection -->
## Procedure

1. Determine `baseSha..headSha` for the implementation and any plan path. Direct the reviewer to run `awf context --show invariants --show all-rules --show evidence --show pending $(git diff --name-only ${baseSha}..${headSha})` itself.
<!-- awf:include context-spill -->
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section dispatch-subagent -->
2. {{ if .targetSubagentTools }}Call `subagent_review` with `kind: "code"`. Choose the smallest reliable tier - `small` (narrow, mechanical), `standard` (substantive but bounded), or `large` (broad, intricate, cross-cutting, or high-consequence) - escalating after uncertainty, failed reasoning, or widened scope; omit the `model` field to use configured role routing, overriding deliberately with the tier's exact `provider/model-id`. Never pass `default`, `auto`, or `inherit parent` as a model value.{{ else }}Dispatch the `code-reviewer` subagent. Choose the smallest reliable tier - `small` (narrow, mechanical), `standard` (substantive but bounded), or `large` (broad, intricate, cross-cutting, or high-consequence) - escalating after uncertainty, failed reasoning, or widened scope; select the smallest reliable target-native model explicitly, or use the harness default and note in the dispatch brief that explicit selection is unavailable.{{ end }} Full tier definitions: docs/working-with-awf.md. Give it a self-contained brief with requested outcome, user constraints, implementation summary, commit range, and verification results. When an effort exists, additionally provide its fixed slug and owned memory evidence read-only, with decision-log entries pasted verbatim including whatever `Record:` blocks exist. Effort-free review creates no effort, memory, checkpoint, retrospective, or topology work.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section classify-route-findings -->
3. Classify findings as mechanical, reasoned, or user-decision and resolve them under repository authority.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section apply-fixes-commit -->
4. Apply authority-determined fixes in new commits and run the required gate.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section run-audit -->
5. Run `awf audit ${baseSha}..${headSha}` after findings settle.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section re-review-loop -->
6. Run one verify pass only when a reasoned or user-decision ruling required a fix. {{ if .targetSubagentTools }}Call `subagent_review` using the same smallest-reliable-tier rule: Choose the smallest reliable tier - `small` (narrow, mechanical), `standard` (substantive but bounded), or `large` (broad, intricate, cross-cutting, or high-consequence), escalating after uncertainty, failed reasoning, or widened scope; omit the `model` field to use configured role routing, overriding deliberately with the tier's exact `provider/model-id`. Never pass `default`, `auto`, or `inherit parent` as a model value.{{ else }}Dispatch the `code-reviewer` with the same smallest-reliable-tier rule: Choose the smallest reliable tier - `small` (narrow, mechanical), `standard` (substantive but bounded), or `large` (broad, intricate, cross-cutting, or high-consequence), escalating after uncertainty, failed reasoning, or widened scope; select the smallest reliable target-native model explicitly, or use the harness default and note in the dispatch brief that explicit selection is unavailable.{{ end }} Full tier definitions: docs/working-with-awf.md.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section hand-off -->
7. Return settled assurance. Effort-backed work returns to `{{ .prefix }}-effort-workflow`; effort-free work concludes after assurance.
<!-- awf:end -->

<!-- awf:section notes -->
## Notes

The reviewer remains report-only and does not edit or commit.
<!-- awf:end -->
